# Valgrind suppressions for the helgrind and DRD runs of prog_fuzz.py
# (--helgrind RTDIR / --drd RTDIR build programs and runtime at -O0
# without inlining, so these frames are visible).
#
# Neither tool models C11 atomics: the runtime's reference counts (String,
# rc, closure environments and cells, and the shared Mutex, Channel,
# RWLock and Arena handles of spawned tasks), the one-time initialization
# of string literals (_iron_lit_N_get) and the generation counters
# synchronize through atomic_* operations with acquire / release ordering,
# which the tools see as plain accesses (ThreadSanitizer, which models
# them, runs the same programs clean). glibc's reuse of cached thread
# stacks is a known helgrind and DRD false positive.

{
   helgrind-glibc-thread-stack-cache
   Helgrind:Race
   ...
   fun:get_cached_stack
}
{
   helgrind-glibc-allocate-stack
   Helgrind:Race
   ...
   fun:allocate_stack
}
{
   helgrind-atomic-_iron_lit_N_get
   Helgrind:Race
   ...
   fun:_iron_lit_*_get
}
{
   helgrind-atomic-iron_string_retain
   Helgrind:Race
   ...
   fun:iron_string_retain
}
{
   helgrind-atomic-iron_string_release
   Helgrind:Race
   ...
   fun:iron_string_release
}
{
   helgrind-atomic-iron__str_free
   Helgrind:Race
   ...
   fun:iron__str_free
}
